==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=fabric|net<id:mesh>|work<id:employment>|tree=1}}
From {{com|en|net|work}}; the nonliteral sense and its subsenses are extended from the literal sense; they are now the dominant senses. Cognate with {{cog|de|Netzwerk}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈnɛt.wɜːk/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈnɛt.wɝk/|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-network.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛtwɜː(ɹ)k|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|any interconnected group or system}} Any [[interconnect]]ed group or system.
#: {{ux|en|A '''network''' of roads crisscrossed the country.}}
#: {{ux|en|The many species that live in the forest canopy constitute a '''network''' of life via their complex interactions.}}
## A set of people with [[sociocultural]] connections to one another; especially, such a set consisting of [[occupational]] or [[business]] connections.
##: {{ux|en|To get a job in today's economy, it is important to have a strong '''network'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|For people with mental health challenges, having a support '''network''' of family and friends can improve the chances of maintaining successful mental health care.}}
## {{senseid|en|Q141683}}{{lb|en|broadcasting}} A group of [[affiliated]] [[television]] stations that [[broadcast]] common [[program]]s from a parent company.
##* '''2008''', Lou Schuler, "Foreward", ''in'' Nate Green, ''Built for Show'', page xi
##*: TV back then was five channels (three '''networks''', PBS, and an independent station that ran ''I Love Lucy'' reruns),{{...}}
## {{senseid|en|Q1301371}} {{lb|en|computing|Internet}} A [[computer network#English:_Q1301371|computer network]]: multiple [[computer]]s and other [[device]]s connected together to share information.
##: {{ux|en|The copy machine is connected to the '''network''' so it can now serve as a printer.}}
# {{senseid|en|fabric or structure of interconnected fibrous elements}} {{lb|en|literal}} A [[fabric]] or [[structure]] of fibrous elements attached to each other at regular intervals; the act or process of making such an object.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=James George Frazer|title=The Golden Bough|year=1911|volume=9|page=287|text=He wore a mantle of '''network'''.}}

